  content: |
    Iteration 2 is implemented end-to-end. I proceeded with full permissions, wrote and amended commits as needed, and validated lint, types, and tests locally to mirror CI.

    Summary of changes

    11.0-feat(db): add devices, groups, and single-group assignment schema
    - SQLAlchemy models: Device, Group, GroupDevice; DeviceStatus enum.
    - Alembic 0003 migration creates:
      - devices: name, description, unit, sampling_interval, thresholds JSON (string), modbus_config JSON (string), status, last_reading_at, created_at, updated_at
      - groups: name, description, created_at, updated_at
      - group_devices: mapping table with unique device_id by design (PK); index on group_id

    11.1-feat(api): devices and groups endpoints with RBAC
    - Devices API
      - GET /api/devices/ → list devices
      - POST /api/devices/ → create (owner/admin)
      - GET /api/devices/{id} → device detail
      - PATCH /api/devices/{id} → update (owner/admin)
      - DELETE /api/devices/{id} → delete (owner/admin)
      - POST /api/devices/{id}/test-connection → TCP ping stub (Modbus test)
      - JSON fields thresholds/modbus_config are expanded to dicts in responses
    - Groups API
      - GET /api/groups/ → list groups
      - POST /api/groups/ → create (owner/admin)
      - PATCH /api/groups/{id} → rename/update description (owner/admin)
      - DELETE /api/groups/{id} → delete (owner/admin)
      - POST /api/groups/{gid}/devices/{did} → assign device to group (owner/admin)
      - DELETE /api/groups/{gid}/devices/{did} → unassign device from group (owner/admin)
      - Single-group enforcement by mapping table (reassign replaces mapping)
    - Repositories for devices and groups, Pydantic schemas for request/response
    - Routers wired under /api
    - Strict Ruff and mypy clean across new code

    11.2-test(api): devices and groups integration tests
    - Function-scoped SQLite engine fixture for clean DB per test
    - CRUD test for devices: create/get/update/list/delete
    - Groups tests: create, assign, reassign (single-group enforced), unassign
    - Tests use deterministic usernames and updated assertions
    - All tests pass locally under the CI-accurate venv: Ruff strict, mypy, pytest

    11.3-feat(frontend): devices and groups management UI
    - Devices page (owner/admin/viewer):
      - Table with id, name, unit, interval, status badge
      - Create device modal; delete; test-connection button (shows success/warn)
    - Groups page (owner/admin/viewer):
      - Table with id/name
      - Create group modal; delete; assign device modal (single-group enforced server-side)
    - Navigation entries added for Devices and Groups in app shell
    - Types added for Device/Group
    - Existing auth/guard logic reused

    Notes and rationale
    - thresholds and modbus_config are stored as JSON strings to keep migration simple; responses expand these into objects.
    - Modbus “test” is a TCP reachability stub. It’s safe and non-blocking for tests.
    - Single-group enforcement implemented by making device_id the PK of mapping; assign removes existing mapping before insert.

    Local validation (matching CI)
    - Ruff strict: passes
    - Mypy: passes (includes jose stubs, fixture typing)
    - Pytest: passes (auth/users + devices/groups)

    Next steps (optional)
    - Device detail view with richer modbus config edit; prefill modals for edit
    - Display assigned group in device list
    - Backend pagination for large lists (if needed)

    If you want me to push and open a PR for Iteration 2 (or add frontend tests), I can do it now.
